  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A square oil painting of flat key or hand shaped forms radiating from a central striped ball, in pastel pink, olive and blue with black outlines.",
    "description": "A square oil painting on canvas. From a small striped sphere at the centre, a dozen flat paddle shapes radiate outward like spokes, each a rounded rectangle with a circular hole and a few hash marks, in olive, cream, grey blue, pink and tan. Thin tapering rods and small ladder like bars run between them. The background is quartered into soft pink, red, orange and lilac. Thick black outlines and white highlight lines, with visible thick paint.",
    "impression": "A wheel of keys, or hands, or heads, all plugged into one hub. The title suggests connection and the picture is a diagram of it, a mind with many ports. It is the most abstract of the Superland paintings and reads like a mandala made of hardware.",
